  "generated_description": "<div class=\"mountain-description prose prose-stone max-w-none\">\n  <p><strong>Applegate Peak</strong> rises to 8,038 feet in Oregon. The Applegate Peak Trail covers 0.7 miles with about 286 feet of elevation gain \u2014 a steady climb. It's rated Easy overall.</p>\n  <h3>The Route</h3><p>The grade is back-loaded: the first half of the route climbs gently, and most of the elevation gain comes in the second half. The steepest stretch arrives around mile 0.53, gaining roughly 2,400 feet per mile \u2014 expect a slow, deliberate pace through here. Along the way the route passes a viewpoint (Phantom Ship Overlook) near mile 0.36, a cliff (Vidae Cliff) near mile 0.56 \u2014 useful checkpoints for judging your pace.</p>\n  <h3>Getting There</h3><p>The trailhead is at <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=42.90001,-122.09571\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">42.90001, -122.09571</a> (tap for driving directions). It's roughly 185 miles south of Portland, Oregon. Arrive early on weekends \u2014 trailhead lots at popular peaks fill quickly, and cell service is often unreliable once you leave the highway.</p>\n  <h3>When to Go</h3><p>Late May through October is the main season. Snow and ice linger into spring and return early in fall at this latitude and elevation; in winter this becomes a different, more serious undertaking requiring traction devices and warm layers.</p>\n  <h3>Know Before You Go</h3><p>The Easy rating comes from the National Park Service difficulty formula, which weighs total distance against elevation gain. Most hikers should budget about 0.5 hours of moving time; add margin for breaks, photos and the descent. Download the GPX track from this page before you go \u2014 cell coverage is unreliable in the mountains and a saved route works offline in any GPS app. Conditions change: verify current access, closures and weather with the official land manager before you go. Trail data is sourced from OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).</p>\n  <p>Looking to link objectives or plan a weekend? Nearby summits include Garfield Peak, Cloudcap and The Watchman \u2014 each has its own guide on this site.</p>\n</div>",
